      "level": 1,
      "content": "CI–Validate Alignment",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "> **Status**: Design Proposal > **Date**: 2026-05-17 > **Scope**: Mapping between CI gate tiers and future `validate` tool profiles.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-3",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Principle",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Every CI gate should have a corresponding `validate` profile so that: - Agents can run the same checks locally via `validate <profile>` that CI runs remotely. - The `validate` tool becomes the single source of truth for check definitions. - CI workflow files become thin wrappers that call `validate` profiles.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-5",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Profile Mapping",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
